GTA San Andreas Audio Editor: Inside-Out Architecture & Tool Development Guide
This document provides a comprehensive, deep-dive architectural breakdown of the GTA San Andreas Audio Editor codebase. It is designed both to explain the internal mechanics of the tool and to serve as a foundational blueprint for developers looking to build custom game asset editors or reverse-engineer proprietary file formats.
1. High-Level Architecture Overview
The tool follows a classic Model-View-Controller (MVC) pattern combined with a worker-thread model to maintain UI responsiveness during heavy I/O and cryptographic operations.
